{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011nGJ1pcjuzLSyNH5P6Hys1","type":"tool_result","content":"     1\t# Runtime identity for the agent pods (IRSA). This role belongs to the agent, not to any user:\n     2\t# patients and staff never receive AWS credentials, and revoking this role does not touch theirs.\n     3\tresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"runtime\" {\n     4\t  name                 = \"clinic-agent-runtime\"\n     5\t  max_session_duration = 3600\n     6\t  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({\n     7\t    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n     8\t    Statement = [{\n     9\t      Effect    = \"Allow\"\n    10\t      Principal = { Federated = module.eks.oidc_provider_arn }\n    11\t      Action    = \"sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity\"\n    12\t      Condition = {\n    13\t        StringEquals = {\n    14\t          \"${module.eks.oidc_provider}:sub\" = [\n    15\t            \"system:serviceaccount:clinic-agent:clinic-agent\",\n    16\t            \"system:serviceaccount:clinic-agent:clinic-agent-reminders\",\n    17\t          ]\n    18\t          \"${module.eks.oidc_provider}:aud\" = \"sts.amazonaws.com\"\n    19\t        }\n    20\t      }\n    21\t    }]\n    22\t  })\n    23\t}\n    24\t\n    25\tresource \"aws_iam_role_policy\" \"runtime\" {\n    26\t  name = \"clinic-agent-runtime\"\n    27\t  role = aws_iam_role.runtime.id\n    28\t  policy = jsonencode({\n    29\t    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    30\t    Statement = [\n    31\t      {\n    32\t        Sid      = \"ReadClinicSecrets\"\n    33\t        Effect   = \"Allow\"\n    34\t        Action   = [\"secretsmanager:GetSecretValue\"]\n    35\t        Resource = \"arn:aws:secretsmanager:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:secret:clinic-agent/*\"\n    36\t      },\n    37\t      {\n    38\t        Sid    = \"AgentState\"\n    39\t        Effect = \"Allow\"\n    40\t        Action = [\n    41\t          \"dynamodb:GetItem\",\n    42\t          \"dynamodb:BatchGetItem\",\n    43\t          \"dynamodb:PutItem\",\n    44\t          \"dynamodb:UpdateItem\",\n    45\t          \"dynamodb:Query\",\n    46\t        ]\n    47\t        Resource = \"arn:aws:dynamodb:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:table/clinic-agent-*\"\n    48\t      },\n    49\t      {\n    50\t        Sid      = \"Audit\"\n    51\t        Effect   = \"Allow\"\n    52\t        Action   = [\"firehose:PutRecord\", \"firehose:PutRecordBatch\"]\n    53\t        Resource = aws_kinesis_firehose_delivery_stream.audit.arn\n    54\t      },\n    55\t    ]\n    56\t  })\n    57\t}\n    58\t\n    59\t# Operators who may stop the agent. Assumable only through SSO by the on-call group.\n    60\tresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"ops_killswitch\" {\n    61\t  name = \"clinic-agent-ops\"\n    62\t  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({\n    63\t    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    64\t    Statement = [{\n    65\t      Effect    = \"Allow\"\n    66\t      Principal = { AWS = \"arn:aws:iam::${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:root\" }\n    67\t      Action    = \"sts:AssumeRole\"\n    68\t      Condition = {\n    69\t        StringLike = { \"aws:PrincipalArn\" = \"arn:aws:iam::${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:role/aws-reserved/sso.amazonaws.com/*/AWSReservedSSO_AgentPlatformOnCall_*\" }\n    70\t      }\n    71\t    }]\n    72\t  })\n    73\t}\n    74\t\n    75\tresource \"aws_iam_role_policy\" \"ops_killswitch\" {\n    76\t  name = \"clinic-agent-ops\"\n    77\t  role = aws_iam_role.ops_killswitch.id\n    78\t  policy = jsonencode({\n    79\t    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    80\t    Statement = [{\n    81\t      Effect   = \"Allow\"\n    82\t      Action   = [\"dynamodb:PutItem\", \"dynamodb:UpdateItem\", \"dynamodb:GetItem\"]\n    83\t      Resource = aws_dynamodb_table.control.arn\n    84\t    }]\n    85\t  })\n    86\t}\n    87\t\n    88\tresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"firehose\" {\n    89\t  name = \"clinic-agent-audit-firehose\"\n    90\t  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({\n    91\t    Version   = \"2012-10-17\"\n    92\t    Statement = [{ Effect = \"Allow\", Principal = { Service = \"firehose.amazonaws.com\" }, Action = \"sts:AssumeRole\" }]\n    93\t  })\n    94\t}\n    95\t\n    96\tresource \"aws_iam_role_policy\" \"firehose\" {\n    97\t  name = \"write-audit-bucket\"\n    98\t  role = aws_iam_role.firehose.id\n    99\t  policy = jsonencode({\n   100\t    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n   101\t    Statement = [{\n   102\t      Effect   = \"Allow\"\n   103\t      Action   = [\"s3:PutObject\", \"s3:AbortMultipartUpload\", \"s3:GetBucketLocation\"]\n   104\t      Resource = [aws_s3_bucket.audit.arn, \"${aws_s3_bucket.audit.arn}/*\"]\n   105\t    }]\n   106\t  })\n   107\t}\n     1\t{\n     2\t  \"name\": \"clinic-agent\",\n     3\t  \"version\": \"3.4.1\",\n     4\t  \"private\": true,\n     5\t  \"type\": \"module\",\n     6\t  \"engines\": {\n     7\t    \"node\": \">=22.11\"\n     8\t  },\n     9\t  \"scripts\": {\n    10\t    \"build\": \"tsc -p tsconfig.json\",\n    11\t    \"start\": \"node dist/server.js\",\n    12\t    \"reminders\": \"node dist/workers/reminders.js\",\n    13\t    \"lint\": \"eslint src test\",\n    14\t    \"test\": \"vitest run\"\n    15\t  },\n    16\t  \"dependencies\": {\n    17\t    \"@anthropic-ai/sdk\": \"0.65.0\",\n    18\t    \"@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb\": \"3.893.0\",\n    19\t    \"@aws-sdk/client-firehose\": \"3.893.0\",\n    20\t    \"@aws-sdk/client-secrets-manager\": \"3.893.0\",\n    21\t    \"@aws-sdk/lib-dynamodb\": \"3.893.0\",\n    22\t    \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk\": \"1.18.2\",\n    23\t    \"fastify\": \"5.6.1\",\n    24\t    \"jose\": \"6.1.0\",\n    25\t    \"pino\": \"9.11.0\",\n    26\t    \"undici\": \"7.16.0\",\n    27\t    \"yaml\": \"2.8.1\",\n    28\t    \"zod\": \"3.25.76\"\n    29\t  },\n    30\t  \"devDependencies\": {\n    31\t    \"@types/node\": \"22.18.6\",\n    32\t    \"eslint\": \"9.36.0\",\n    33\t    \"typescript\": \"5.9.2\",\n    34\t    \"typescript-eslint\": \"8.44.1\",\n    35\t    \"vitest\": \"3.2.4\"\n    36\t  }\n    37\t}\n# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1.7\nFROM node:22.11-bookworm-slim@sha256:3f1a8d2c9b7e4f6a5d0c8b1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f9a0b1c2d3e4f5a6b7c8d9e0f1a AS build\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY package.json package-lock.json ./\nRUN npm ci --ignore-scripts\nCOPY tsconfig.json ./\nCOPY src ./src\nRUN npm run build && npm prune --omit=dev\n\nFROM gcr.io/distroless/nodejs22-debian12:nonroot@sha256:9b2e4c6a8d0f1e3c5a7b9d1f3e5c7a9b1d3f5e7c9a1b3d5f7e9c1a3b5d7f9e1c\nWORKDIR /app\nENV NODE_ENV=production \\\n    CLINIC_AGENT_ROOT=/app\nCOPY --from=build --chown=65532:65532 /app/node_modules ./node_modules\nCOPY --from=build --chown=65532:65532 /app/dist ./dist\nCOPY --chown=65532:65532 package.json ./\nCOPY --chown=65532:65532 prompts ./prompts\nCOPY --chown=65532:65532 config ./config\nCOPY --chown=65532:65532 release ./release\nUSER 65532:65532\nEXPOSE 8080\nCMD [\"dist/server.js\"]\n# Every tool the scheduling agent may call, with the task it serves.\n# The executor denies any tool not listed here. Annotations from servers (readOnlyHint and so on)\n# are not used for allow or approval decisions.\nrole: scheduling_agent\ntools:\n  - tool: ehr__find_patient\n    reason: Match the sender to a patient record by date of birth and phone or email.\n  - tool: ehr__search_slots\n    reason: List open slots for a provider, location, and visit type.\n  - tool: ehr__get_appointment\n    reason: Read one appointment the patient asks about.\n  - tool: ehr__list_patient_appointments\n    reason: Show the patient their upcoming appointments.\n  - tool: ehr__book_appointment\n    reason: Book a slot the patient chose.\n  - tool: ehr__update_appointment\n    reason: Change time, provider, or status (confirmed / checked_in / no_show / cancelled) of an appointment.\n  - tool: ehr__cancel_appointment\n    reason: Cancel an appointment at the patient's request.\n  - tool: payments__refund_deposit\n    reason: Refund a no-show deposit after staff review.\n  - tool: sms__send_to_patient\n    reason: Send a templated message to the phone number on the patient's record.\n  - tool: sms__send_freeform\n    reason: Send a staff-approved message that is not one of the templates.\n  - tool: insurance__check_eligibility\n    reason: Ask the eligibility agent whether a visit is covered.\n{\n  \"brace_checklist\": \"2026-10-01\",\n  \"repo\": \"\",\n  \"commit\": null,\n  \"reviewed_at\": \"2026-10-20T13:58:13Z\",\n  \"scope\": \"TODO: what was reviewed and what wasn't.\",\n  \"review_protocol\": \"coverage-first-v1\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"item\": \"A05\",\n      \"gate\": \"G1\",\n      \"title\": \"Operational lookup\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Start from one suspicious action. Find the team responsible, the current operator, the deployment manifest, and the live instance. Show that you can contain the right instance or agent type without cutting off the launching user's other access.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Stop doesn't halt running work or open tool streams within a set time\",\n          \"owner\": \"R11\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"No drill for a compromised shared tool or agent type\",\n          \"owner\": \"E12\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Action records missing any of the six identity fields\",\n          \"owner\": \"A02\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"needs_evidence\",\n      \"confidence\": \"low\",\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A05.1\",\n          \"check\": \"Each audit record carries the agent-type-id and agent-instance-id, which resolve to a stored deployment manifest and a live instance.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Open the audit record writer. 2) Check `agent.type.id` and `agent.instance.id` are written on every record. 3) Check the type ID can be looked up to a stored manifest (registry, manifest store, file keyed by hash). 4) Answer no if either field is missing or nothing stores manifests by that ID. Answer unknown if the lookup store is outside this repo.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"\",\n          \"quote\": \"\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A05.2\",\n          \"check\": \"An ownership record in code or config maps each agent type to a responsible team and a current operator or on-call rotation.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Look for CODEOWNERS, `catalog-info.yaml`, `.brace/deployment.yaml`, or another ownership file. 2) Check each agent type maps to a team and to a current operator or on-call rotation. 3) Answer no if an agent type has no owner, or owners exist only in prose with no link. Answer unknown if ownership lives in an outside catalog.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"\",\n          \"quote\": \"\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A05.3\",\n          \"check\": \"A containment control can disable a single instance or a single agent type (for example revoke its principal or scale it to zero) without touching the launching user's credentials.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find stop and revoke controls: admin endpoints, CLIs, feature flags, scale-to-zero, per-instance","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7a6e11a-0cdc-487a-a909-76d22aa8270a","uuid":"8d2bb28c-87ef-4de9-9311-de7302993e55","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:59:00.575Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"     1\t# Runtime identity for the agent pods (IRSA). This role belongs to the agent, not to any user:\n     2\t# patients and staff never receive AWS credentials, and revoking this role does not t