{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015iLzr7hHMJPd5MR35ScXxJ","type":"tool_result","content":"     1\timport type Anthropic from \"@anthropic-ai/sdk\";\n     2\t\n     3\t// Context size at decision time, in tokens.\n     4\t//\n     5\t// Counting method. Each model decision is one Messages API call. Its response usage reports the\n     6\t// prompt of that single call in three parts: input_tokens (uncached), cache_read_input_tokens, and\n     7\t// cache_creation_input_tokens. Their sum is the full prompt the model read for this decision,\n     8\t// including the part served from the prompt cache and the provider's own tool-use preamble, which\n     9\t// the provider counts but does not show. This is a per-call value, not a run or billing total.\n    10\t// We record it as \"measured\", with the cached share kept separately.\n    11\t//\n    12\t// If the response carries no usage (stream cut off, aborted call), we fall back to the\n    13\t// count_tokens estimate taken just before the call for the same request, and mark it \"estimated\".\n    14\t// If neither exists the value is null with status \"unavailable\". It is never reported as 0.\n    15\t//\n    16\t// This harness never compacts, summarizes, or truncates history inside a run, so compacted is\n    17\t// always false; a run that would outgrow its token budget stops instead (see budget.ts).\n    18\texport interface ContextSize {\n    19\t  tokens: number | null;\n    20\t  status: \"measured\" | \"estimated\" | \"unavailable\";\n    21\t  method: string;\n    22\t  cachedInputTokens: number | null;\n    23\t  compacted: boolean;\n    24\t}\n    25\t\n    26\texport const USAGE_METHOD = \"anthropic.messages.usage(input+cache_read+cache_creation)\";\n    27\texport const COUNT_METHOD = \"anthropic.messages.count_tokens(pre-call estimate)\";\n    28\t\n    29\texport async function measureBeforeCall(\n    30\t  client: Anthropic,\n    31\t  req: Anthropic.MessageCountTokensParams,\n    32\t  signal: AbortSignal,\n    33\t): Promise<ContextSize> {\n    34\t  try {\n    35\t    const r = await client.messages.countTokens(req, { signal });\n    36\t    return { tokens: r.input_tokens, status: \"estimated\", method: COUNT_METHOD, cachedInputTokens: null, compacted: false };\n    37\t  } catch {\n    38\t    return { tokens: null, status: \"unavailable\", method: COUNT_METHOD, cachedInputTokens: null, compacted: false };\n    39\t  }\n    40\t}\n    41\t\n    42\texport function completeFromUsage(pre: ContextSize, usage: Anthropic.Usage | undefined | null): ContextSize {\n    43\t  if (!usage) return pre;\n    44\t  const cacheRead = usage.cache_read_input_tokens ?? 0;\n    45\t  const total = usage.input_tokens + cacheRead + (usage.cache_creation_input_tokens ?? 0);\n    46\t  return { tokens: total, status: \"measured\", method: USAGE_METHOD, cachedInputTokens: cacheRead, compacted: false };\n    47\t}\n    48\t\n    49\t// Span attributes so the value is searchable next to the action in traces as well as audit.\n    50\texport function spanAttributes(c: ContextSize): Record<string, string | number | boolean> {\n    51\t  return {\n    52\t    ...(c.tokens === null ? {} : { \"clinic_agent.context.tokens\": c.tokens }),\n    53\t    \"clinic_agent.context.status\": c.status,\n    54\t    \"clinic_agent.context.method\": c.method,\n    55\t    \"gen_ai.conversation.compacted\": c.compacted,\n    56\t  };\n    57\t}\n(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*.ts\ntest/controls.test.ts:97:  const reply = (model: string, text: string) => async () => ({ model, content: [{ type: \"text\", text }] });\ntest/controls.test.ts:109:  it(\"treats a swapped served model as a control failure\", async () => {\ntest/controls.test.ts:111:    expect(d).toMatchObject({ route: \"staff\", failure: \"model_mismatch\", servedModel: \"claude-haiku-4-5\" });\nA05 {\"gate\": \"G1\", \"title\": \"Operational lookup\", \"lead_role\": \"operations\", \"requirement\": \"Start from one suspicious action. Find the team responsible, the current operator, the deployment manifest, and the live instance. Show that you can contain the right instance or agent type without cutting off the launching user's other access.\", \"not_covered\": [{\"problem\": \"Stop doesn't halt running work or open tool streams within a set time\", \"owner\": \"R11\"}, {\"problem\": \"No drill for a compromised shared tool or agent type\", \"owner\": \"E12\"}, {\"problem\": \"Action records missing any of the six identity fields\", \"owner\": \"A02\"}], \"na_when\": \"never\", \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"A05.1\", \"check\": \"Each audit record carries the agent-type-id and agent-instance-id, which resolve to a stored deployment manifest and a live instance.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Open the audit record writer. 2) Check `agent.type.id` and `agent.instance.id` are written on every record. 3) Check the type ID can be looked up to a stored manifest (registry, manifest store, file keyed by hash). 4) Answer no if either field is missing or nothing stores manifests by that ID. Answer unknown if the lookup store is outside this repo.\"}, {\"id\": \"A05.2\", \"check\": \"An ownership record in code or config maps each agent type to a responsible team and a current operator or on-call rotation.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Look for CODEOWNERS, `catalog-info.yaml`, `.brace/deployment.yaml`, or another ownership fi\nA06 {\"gate\": \"G3\", \"title\": \"Parent and prompt provenance\", \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\", \"requirement\": \"For every sub-agent, record its own type and instance IDs, a link to its parent, trace links, and the prompt the parent gave it. Trace a nested action back to that prompt. Protect sensitive prompt text with restricted storage and a clear redaction policy. Standard GenAI instrumentation records prompts only when you turn that on, so confirm it is on for this path.\", \"not_covered\": [{\"problem\": 