{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CgTyktvmN5v4j8fooQSukk","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"id\": \"A07.1\",\n  \"check\": \"A model inventory in code or config lists every helper model the agent calls (verifiers, judges, rerankers, embedding models, world models).\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Search for every model call: provider SDK clients, model name strings, embedding, rerank, moderation, and judge calls. 2) Compare that list with the model inventory. 3) Answer no if any helper model called in code is missing from the inventory, or no inventory exists.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n----\n{\n  \"id\": \"A07.2\",\n  \"check\": \"Each helper model is identified by a pinned version or digest plus its prompt and configuration, not by an alias.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) For each helper model, find its model ID and follow env vars to the final value. 2) Check it is a pinned version or digest, and that its prompt and configuration are also recorded. 3) Answer no if any is an alias (`-latest`, undated name), falls back to one by default, or is hard-coded inline outside the inventory.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n----\n{\n  \"id\": \"A07.3\",\n  \"check\": \"Each helper model's decisions are logged with that model's identity.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Open each helper or checker call site. 2) Check its decision is logged with that model's ID and version. 3) Answer no if decisions are logged without model identity, or logged only on the allow or success branch.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n----\n{\n  \"id\": \"A07.4\",\n  \"check\": \"A checker timeout, error, invalid output, or version mismatch makes the control that depends on it fail (block or escalate), not pass by default.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Open each checker call site (judge, guardrail, moderation, verifier). 2) Read every `try/except`, `catch`, timeout, and parse-error branch. 3) Check each one blocks or escalates. 4) Answer no if any branch returns allow, skips the check, treats unparseable output as safe, or logs and continues. Also no if the returned model version is never compared with the expected one.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n----\n{\n  \"id\": \"C01.3\",\n  \"check\": \"Each requested model ID is labeled as a pinned snapshot or a changeable alias, with the provider doc and date used.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Open each model record in the manifest. 2) Check it has a pinned-or-alias label, the provider doc used, and a date. 3) Answer no if any record lacks one of these, or labels an undated or `-latest` name as pinned.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n----\n{\n  \"id\": \"C02.1\",\n  \"check\": \"The manifest, prompts, tool config, and policy files live in version control, and merges require review by someone other than the named author.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Check the manifest, prompts, tool config, and policy files are tracked in git, not loaded at runtime from an untracked path or remote URL. 2) Look for branch protection or ruleset config requiring approving review, and CODEOWNERS covering those paths. 3) Answer no if any of these files is untracked or not covered. Answer unknown if review rules are set only in the hosting service.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n----\nusage: answer.py [-h] [--repo REPO] [--met {yes,no,unknown}] [--evidence EVIDENCE] [--quote QUOTE] [--counter COUNTER] [--note NOTE]\n                 [--rating {likely_pass,gap,needs_evidence,na_candidate}] [--confidence {high,medium,low}] [--summary SUMMARY] [--next NEXT_STEP] [--violates VIOLATES]\n                 [--also-affects ALSO_AFFECTS] [--verdict {confirmed,dismissed}] [--item ITEM] [--reason REASON]\n                 findings {check,flag,item,prescan,next} [target]\n\nWrite one answer into a findings file, check it, and show what's next.\n\nUse this instead of editing the JSON by hand.\n\n  Answer a check:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json check B05.2 --met no --evidence src/x.py:41 \\\n        --quote \"exact code on that line\" --note \"what the code does\" [--counter \"what you searched\"]\n\n  Add a red flag:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json flag B05 --evidence src/x.py:41 --note \"what's wrong\"\n\n  Finish an item:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json item B05 --rating gap --confidence high \\\n        --summary \"one sentence\" --next \"what to fix\" [--violates \"exact words from the requirement\"] \\\n        [--also-affects E06]\n\n  Resolve a pre-scan hit:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json prescan H003 --verdict confirmed --item R03 --reason \"...\"\n\n  Show the next unanswered check:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json next\n\nThe quote is checked against the file right away; a \"yes\" without a matching quote\nand a counter-search is refused. Paths are relative to the repo, which defaults to the\nfolder holding FINDINGS.json (set --repo to change it).\nusage: review_coverage.py ledger [-h] --rows ROWS [--attempts ATTEMPTS] [--deviations DEVIATIONS] findings check\n\npositional arguments:\n  findings\n  check\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --rows ROWS\n  --attempts ATTEMPTS\n  --deviations DEVIATIONS","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7a6e11a-0cdc-487a-a909-76d22aa8270a","uuid":"7e3a45a6-e433-4374-adab-20e9c15f660d","timestamp":"2026-10-20T14:00:23.295Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"id\": \"A07.1\",\n  \"check\": \"A model inventory in code or config lists every helper model the agent calls (verifiers, judges, rerankers, embedding models, world models).\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Search for every model call: provider SDK clients, model name strings, embedding, rerank, moderation, and judge calls. 2) Compare that list with the model inventory. 3) Answer no if any helper model calle