{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WMJswFtGHZgeh1Rn7fTa9d","type":"tool_result","content":"Saved A05.1 = no. Next: A05.2 — An ownership record in code or config maps each agent type to a responsible team and a current operator or on-call rotation.\n  How to verify: 1) Look for CODEOWNERS, `catalog-info.yaml`, `.brace/deployment.yaml`, or another ownership file. 2) Check each agent type maps to a team and to a current operator or on-call rotation. 3) Answer no if an agent type has no owner, or owners exist only in prose with no link. Answer unknown if ownership lives in an outside catalog.\nSaved A05.2 = no. Next: A05.3 — A containment control can disable a single instance or a single agent type (for example revoke its principal or scale it to zero) without touching the launching user's credentials.\n  How to verify: 1) Find stop and revoke controls: admin endpoints, CLIs, feature flags, scale-to-zero, per-instance token revocation. 2) Check their scope is one instance or one agent type. 3) Answer no if the only control is a global switch or revoking a shared or user credential. Answer unknown if containment is run by an outside platform.\nSaved A05.3 = no. Next: finish item A05 with `answer.py ... item A05 --rating ...`\nAdded red flag to A05.\nSaved item A05 = gap. Next: A06.1 — Each sub-agent gets its own type ID and instance ID, assigned by the harness when it is started.\n  How to verify: 1) Find sub-agent spawn code (handoffs, subgraphs, subagents, A2A task creation). 2) Check the harness assigns the child a new `agent.instance.id` and a type ID at start. 3) Answer no if any spawn path reuses the parent's IDs, assigns none, or takes the IDs from the model's request.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7a6e11a-0cdc-487a-a909-76d22aa8270a","uuid":"c705afaa-c498-4cfb-91fd-53132dcbf853","timestamp":"2026-10-20T14:01:06.595Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Saved A05.1 = no. Next: A05.2 — An ownership record in code or config maps each agent type to a responsible team and a current operator or on-call rotation.\n  How to verify: 1) Look for CODEOWNERS, `catalog-info.yaml`, `.brace/deployment.yaml`, or another ownership file. 2) Check each agent type maps to a team and to a current operator or on-call rotation. 3) Answer no if an agent type has no owner, or owners exist only in prose with no link. Answer unknown if ownership lives in an outside catalog.\nSaved A05.2 = no. Next: A05.3 — A containment control can disable a single instance or a single agent type (for example revoke its principal or scale it to zero) without touching the launching user's credentials.\n  How to verify: 1) Find stop and revoke controls: admin endpoints, CLIs, feature flags, scale-to-zero, per-instance token revocation. 2) Check their scope is one instance or one agent type. 3) Answer no if the only control is a global switch or revoking a shared or user credential. Answer unknown if containment is run by an outside platform.\nSaved A05.3 = no. Next: finish item A05 with `answer.py ... item A05 --rating ...`\nAdded red flag to A05.\nSaved item A05 = gap. Next: A06.1 — Each sub-agent gets its own type ID and instance ID, assigned by the harness when it is started.\n  How to verify: 1) Find sub-agent spawn code (handoffs, subgraphs, subagents, A2A task creation). 2) Check the harness assigns the child a new `agent.instance.id` and a type ID at start. 3) Answer no if any spawn path reuses the parent's IDs, assigns none, or takes the IDs from the model's request.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WMJswFtGHZgeh1Rn7fTa9d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
