{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDcUXbiePLLfxUkvFcgX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed A05, A06, A07, C01 and C02 and saved the results to `agent/brace-findings.json`. Four items are gaps and A07 is a likely_pass. The batch validation with `--before-challenges` printed `Valid`. I did not run challenges and I executed nothing from the fixture.\n\n| Item | Rating | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| A05 Operational lookup | gap | The only stop control is a DynamoDB halt flag at global or per-clinic scope (`src/control/kill-switch.ts:28`), so one instance or agent type can't be contained alone. The reminder job never compares its type ID to the manifest and never logs its instance ID (`src/workers/reminders.ts:13`). The operator is one hardcoded string (`src/config.ts:64`), and the on-call rotation exists only in README prose. |\n| A06 Parent and prompt provenance | gap | I treated the A2A call to the eligibility peer as a delegated agent task. It has no harness-assigned IDs, no parent instance ID (only `traceparent`, `eligibility-a2a.ts:61`), and no captured prompt. Its result can trigger a refund (`eligibility-check.ts:40`). |\n| A07 Every model in the loop | likely_pass | The classifier is the only helper model. It is pinned to a dated snapshot, and its ID hashes the model, prompt and config. Every decision is logged, and every failure or model mismatch routes to staff. |\n| C01 Release manifest | gap | The manifest has no issuer/audience bindings or MCP versions. Only the EHR MCP server and the eligibility peer have owners. Two checks are unknown: C01.2 (no separate exact-version field) and C01.5 (training could live in another repo). |\n| C02 Review of changes | gap | The emergency path in `deploy.yml:50` accepts an empty or relative `expires_on`, because GNU `date -d` treats those as valid. I didn't run `date`, so that rests on how GNU date behaves. The catch-all `*` owner in CODEOWNERS covers `src/config.ts`, which holds production model IDs and endpoints. |\n\n- **Prescan:** none of the 11 hits belong to these five items. They are B11, B02, R13 and E03 hits, and I left them for those batches.\n- **A06 call:** if governance reads the peer as not a sub-agent, A06 would become a not-applicable candidate instead.\n- **C02.1 caveat:** the fixture has no `.git`, so I couldn't confirm the files are tracked. The \"yes\" rests on the Terraform branch protection and CODEOWNERS.\n\nThe scope field in the file records these limits."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":742,"cache_read_input_tokens":97723,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":742},"output_tokens":759,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7a6e11a-0cdc-487a-a909-76d22aa8270a","uuid":"4754ca6e-5d87-421e-9f6a-33d8c805540f","timestamp":"2026-10-20T14:02:20.276Z","request_id":"req_011CgDcUXK7kRG49LyRw6GC6"}
